| S. Akella, A. Gadde, J. Pandey, *Multi-invariants in stabilizer states*, arXiv:2601.16258v1, §3.1 and §5 | `literature-attested`: the Rényi entropies of a stabilizer state across a bipartition do not depend on the Rényi index (§3.1; Remark 3.3); for $\mathtt q=3$ and every replica index, the Rényi multi-entropy of a stabilizer state is given in §5 in terms of orders of stabilizer subgroups, via the GHZ-extraction theorem. The GHZ-extraction method for tripartite invariants and the resulting $n\to1$ multi-entropy formula are due to S. Akella, *Tripartite entanglement in the HaPPY code is not holographic*, arXiv:2510.08520v1, §3.2, Eq. (31), which treats only the limit $n\to1$; the formula for every replica index is the one in §5 of arXiv:2601.16258. This is the literature status of the values in the case $\mathtt q=3$ of Theorem 3.1 and Corollary 4.2; arXiv:2601.16258 states no rank formula over $\mathbb F_2(\zeta)$ and treats no $\mathtt q\ge4$ at $n\ge3$. Its multi-entropy normalisation omits the factor $n^{2-\mathtt q}$, which is immaterial for $\mathtt q\le2$ and a constant factor for $\mathtt q=3$. 